              "text": "гусь (gus) — \"a goose\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гусь (gus) from Proto-Slavic gǫsĭ. If it were inherited from the Indo-European word for \"goose\", Slavic would have з-, as Lithuanian žąsìs, Latin ānser and German Gans lead one to expect; so its г- is explained in several ways, among them a Germanic loan (Vasmer)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
